Bar is a minimal status bar for the River Wayland compositor,
written in Zig.

WHAT IS BAR?

Bar draws itself with a built-in 9x15 bitmap font and the standard
Wayland shared-memory buffers. It shows the tags of every output,
a clock, and any status text you feed it on standard input. It has
no dependencies beyond libwayland and the Wayland protocols the
compositor itself uses.

BUILDING

You need Zig and libwayland-devel.

        zig build -Doptimize=ReleaseFast

The binary lands in zig-out/bin/bar.

RUNNING

By itself it shows the tags and the clock:

        ./zig-out/bin/bar

Feed it status text on stdin to get a status section:

        while true; do echo "$(uptime)"; sleep 1; done | ./zig-out/bin/bar

Start it from your River configuration:

        riverctl spawn "sh -c 'while true; do bstatus; sleep 1;
                     done | /path/to/bar'"

Note that riverctl spawn runs the command from the compositor's
working directory and discards its output. Use an absolute path.

DEBUGGING

When you have no Wayland screenshot tool, set BAR_DUMP to a file
and the first drawn frame is written there as raw ARGB pixels:

        BAR_DUMP=/tmp/bar.argb ./zig-out/bin/bar

LAYOUT

The bar, left to right: the tags of each output as digit blocks
(focused inverted, urgent red), the date and time, then the status
text from standard input.

The source tree:

  src/        the bar
  protocol/   vendored Wayland protocol definitions
  build.zig   the build plumbing

